      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T17:33:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, only with pvIOMMU we use did\u003dFLPT_DEFAULT_DID as the criteria for whether to use the host EPT or not? With the old shadow IOMMU implementation we use different criteria (i.e. translation type set to passthrough in the host\u0027s virtual context or PASID entry), and we allow the host to set any did in this case (so we cannot trust the host that it will set FLPT_DEFAULT_DID)?\n\nSo maybe don\u0027t remove the existing implementation of pkvm_iommu_flush_iotlb() but keep it, but add the new one under #ifdef CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL_PVIOMMU?",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52f987fe_0913c933",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-26T03:07:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the case of shadow, we can put a check in the hypervisor to make sure that host always sets the passthrough mode with FLPT_DEFAULT_DID. It is a fairly simple change and will avoid two implementations.",
      "parentUuid": "69b07cc2_09fc8709",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22ffb5bc_4a2fcc5f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-26T11:47:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, but adding #ifdef is not difficult either, and would avoid changing the way how shadow IOMMU works (since changing it is not our goal)? And as I see it, \"conceptually\", what the shadow IOMMU implementation does is emulating the IOMMU for the host to let it use the IOMMU in more or less arbitrary ways, with (almost) no assumptions about how exactly the host IOMMU driver uses it. Whereas in pvIOMMU, pKVM closely cooperates with the host IOMMU driver, so in case of pvIOMMU it does make sense to use FLPT_DEFAULT_DID as the criterion.\n\nWell, the shadow IOMMU implementation is going away anyway (we will not port it to v6.18 and so on), so basically I\u0027m fine either way.",
      "parentUuid": "52f987fe_0913c933",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
