      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T01:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "__submit_qi(iommu, \u0026desc, 1) already takes the iommu-\u003eqi_lock.",
      "parentUuid": "6d6a9fd4_58a7a580",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd4389ce_bf87ff0b",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2407,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T18:12:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed... and at least at first glance at the code in __submit_qi(), it seems it should be safe to call it without iommu-\u003elock locked.\n\nThis gives me some thoughts:\n1. Looks like in the old shadow IOMMU implementation, locking iommu-\u003eqi_lock was always done with iommu-\u003elock locked. Which makes it unclear why iommu-\u003eqi_lock was needed in the first place.\n2. In the new pvIOMMU implementation, I see it\u0027s different: we do QI flushing after unlocking iommu-\u003elock, following what the host IOMMU driver does. That probably makes sense, yeah, and may be good for performance.\n\n...So, yeah, it seems safe to not lock iommu-\u003elock here. OTOH, if we add checking if there are any passthrough domains (to avoid unneeded flushing if there are none), as we discussed below, then we will need to lock iommu-\u003elock here?\n\nAnd it seems this extra locking here shouldn\u0027t be a big problem then: although we might have a lock contention here e.g. when donating pages to a pVM in parallel on multiple CPUs, but we have this contention anyway, since we lock iommu-\u003eqi_lock anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "b11145d4_f6e9cf07",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9fb80f3_680892fc",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2407,
      "author": {
        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T01:23:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am using an `atomic_t` type counter, so we won\u0027t to take iommu-\u003elock.",
      "parentUuid": "bd4389ce_bf87ff0b",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f51495ad_bef33d18",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2416,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T18:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This descriptor will be submitted even if there are no devices with FLPT_DEFAULT_DID on this IOMMU (e.g. with default IOMMU mode set to strict or lazy). Can we optimize that?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "683c16e1_5802a9c0",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 2399,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 2399,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\nstatic bool iommu_has_default_did_ptdev(struct pkvm_iommu *iommu)\n{\n\tstruct pkvm_ptdev *p;\n\n\tpkvm_spin_lock(\u0026iommu-\u003elock);\n\tlist_for_each_entry(p, \u0026iommu-\u003eptdev_head, iommu_node) {\n\t\tif (p-\u003edid \u003d\u003d FLPT_DEFAULT_DID) {\n\t\t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026iommu-\u003elock);\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026iommu-\u003elock);\n\treturn false;\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 2408,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 2408,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\t/*\n\t\t * Only submit the descriptor if there is at least one device\n\t\t * associated with FLPT_DEFAULT_DID on this IOMMU.\n\t\t */\n\t\tif (!iommu_has_default_did_ptdev(iommu))\n\t\t\tcontinue;\n\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f2731c5_801c4460",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
