      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T02:07:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it a good idea to add a boolean field in `struct pkvm_iommu` which gets set to true when atleast one domain in it is passthrough? Then while doing the flush, we can check this field and only do flush when that field is set.",
      "parentUuid": "f51495ad_bef33d18",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "081f5fd0_48c222b5",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2416,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T18:12:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You mean, just to avoid iterating the list of devices here every time?\n\nI guess it would be not a boolean but a counter, i.e. we would just check if this counter is non-zero?\n\nSeems not a bad idea. Although I guess it would require a bit of extra complexity to maintain this counter when updating a context or PASID entry (and as one Linux kernel maintainer once said, \"more state, more problems\"), but maybe let\u0027s try.",
      "parentUuid": "7f2731c5_801c4460",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3725a7d1_dc4a8359",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2416,
      "author": {
        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T18:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case of PVIOMMU, the list doesn\u0027t contain anything, as we don\u0027t need it. It\u0027s a remnant from shadow impl. I should put a #ifdef PVIOMMU around it. \n\nRight, it will be a counter, since the devices can be added/removed. I also feel, it will add a bit of complexity, but seems a straight forward solution for now.",
      "parentUuid": "081f5fd0_48c222b5",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca6301c1_bdb9a4a8",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 2416,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T19:32:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In case of PVIOMMU, the list doesn\u0027t contain anything, as we don\u0027t need it. It\u0027s a remnant from shadow impl.\n\nAh, indeed. Then, a counter might be actually the simplest way to implement avoiding unneeded flushing.\n\nWhich seems worth implementing anyway. I didn\u0027t specifically measure how long a QI submit takes, but I doubt it is blazingly fast. And I did see page fault handling for a pVM taking on average several times longer than for a npVM, and my only working theory is that it is due to these IOTLB flushes during page donation.",
      "parentUuid": "3725a7d1_dc4a8359",
      "revId": "40c13d07570e31913e85ee9cc07332d4a5a90e80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
